 say hey!
 I think finally we all know for sure which startup in our class generated the biggest return. It was pretty close there for a minute, Nick and I thought we were gonna walk away with it until that big IPO pop yesterday. So the time has come
 to say congrats to the Airbeds!
 I was reading Einar's and Gabor's and Tom's and Dan's comments throughout the web this morning and watch Brian's interview on Bloomberg (cmon toughen up ya big softy), and was just reflecting that the 2008-2009 time period was a
 very transformative year for me, and it was nice to read about other people's experiences to remind me that that crazy time did indeed happen.
 I thought it would be fun sometime to do a zoom reunion call and share exaggerated tales of how we all were the true cause of Airbnb's success. I am still just a programmer though and not a PM, so will take no initiative in making
 something like that happen.
 Anyway, congrats Nate, Joe & Brian! Very proud to be a part of that class, and inspired to see that it is true that "Integrity and Perseverance in Business ensure success".
 Also mahalo to the shoddy admissions committee at Combinator for letting me sneak in.
 Aloha!
