id hair-stand-on-end
title Spend Slowly Because the World Is Unpredictable
year 2015
source Jessica Livingston
kind email
image hairStandOnEnd.png
transcript
 [ycfounders - confidential] "Spend slowly because the world is
 unpredictable" >
 YCFounders x
 Jessica Livingston <x@ycombinator.com>
 to ycfounders -
 Unsubscribe
 Thu, Aug 13, 2015, 7:16 PM
 There have been a bunch of high profile startup failures lately. This week's casualty, Zirtual, reminded me how crucial it is not to
 assume raising more money will be as easy as it was the first time. One article, in particular, had a sentence that literally made
 my hair stand on end:
 "Donovan says she wasn't worried because the company had not had trouble raising money before..."
 I urge you all to 1) know how much runway you have before your startup runs out of money, 2) do not think that raising
 additional money is a "given" and 3) do not be in denial about points 1 and 2.
 I wrote about some of this stuff in my blog post, "Subtle Mid-stage Startup Pitfalls" and it's worth reading if only to remind
 yourself that you should spend your money like it's the last you will ever raise.
 Jessica Livingston Partner, Y Combinator
 www.ycombinator.com
 www.foundersatwork.com
