id sama-for-president
title Sama for President
year 2014
source Paul Graham
kind email
image samaForPresident.png
context https://x.com/breckyunits/status/2108164201105776727
transcript
 P
 Lycfounders] Sama for President »
 Founders x
 Paul Graham <pg@ycombinator.com>
 to ycfounders -
 In case you hadn't already heard, Sam Altman is taking over as
 president of YC. Or more precisely, we're going to create the job
 of president and Sam is going to be it. Although I'll continue to
 do office hours with startups, Sam is going to be leading YC.
 This move was a long time in the works. I started trying to recruit
 Sam to take over from me in the summer of 2012, and it took me over
 a year to convince him.
 The reason I wanted Sam to take over was that, as many of you have
 probably realized, I'm not particularly well suited to running a
 large organization. And yet YC is going to need to grow if we're
 going to fund the ever increasing number of startups that will be
 started in the coming years. I knew for YC's sake and my own that
 I needed to find someone to take over. And those of you who know
 Sam will understand why he was my and Jessica's first choice.
 As I was talking with Sam about him taking over I realized something
 kind of exciting: YC could last for a very long time. Product
 companies rarely last as long as 100 years. I suspect it's because
 they embody some assumption about their market that eventually
 becomes false. But YC is fundamentally just a nexus of people,
 like a university. Those can last very long; 100 years is nothing
 for a university.
 I think YC is net good for the world, and it would be pretty cool
 if it lasted a long time. Sam and I are organizing it with that
 in mind, and Clevy is at this moment trying to cook up documents
 that will still work when they're being interpreted by cyborgs a
 few centuries from now. At the very least YC should be increasingly
 able to help you for the next few years.
 × ₴
 Fri, Feb 21, 2014, 2:28PM * • /
 -- pg
