transcript
 - Forwarded message -
 From: Paul Biggar <paul.biggar@gmail.com>
 Date: Thu, Dec 20, 2012 at 6:55 PM
 Subject: Re: [yc-international] Any immigration lawyer suggestion?
 To: yc-international@googlegroups.com
 Welcome!
 A quick tip to the Winter 2013s, which I wish I knew back when I
 joined the list: there is a huge wealth of knowledge in the archives,
 which will provide a great deal of background for how immigration
 looks to founders, specific answers to your questions, and also tell
 you all the things you didn't know to ask.
 https://groups.google.com/forum/#!forum/yc-international
 Now to answer your question: A H1B will be between $4-$8K - expect to
 pay $5.5K including filing fees. I haven't done an 01, but I believe
 its slightly more expensive but in the same ball park.
 The two most commonly recommended lawyers are Chris Wright and Olivia
 Lee. Olivia is all round great, but Chris can pull off miracles (the
 price is that he doesn't answer emails in a timely fashion or hold
 your hand - hence my personal preference for Olivia).
 Happy to intro you to either.
 Paul

