 Mon, Aug 6, 2012, 6:36 AM
 We're looking for someone to moderate Hacker News. It should take
 3-4 hours a day of work, total. The catch is that this time will
 be spread out across the day: you can't go more than about 2 hours
 during the day in the US without checking the site, or bad things
 happen.
 We're looking for someone with good judgment and an understanding
 of the topics people talk about on HN. The person would not have
 to do serious hacking but would have to know how to do stuff like
 grep in log files. (If someone wanted to do some forensic hacking
 to figure out how to make the site faster, that would be fabulous.)
 YC alums would be ideal, if there are any of you looking to make
 some money on the side while working on other projects. Because
 we want someone good, we're willing to pay $6k/month.
 Let me know if you're interested.
 -Pg
